{
 "scene_id": "09.1",
 "poem": "09",
 "title": "Yet, Heard",
 "movement": "THE SHARED MOON",
 "seconds": 17,
 "lines": "accepting you'll never / say nor / ever feel / my love was real\u2014 / what isn't mine, / I still can not give. / I gather my things to go. / before I go\u2014 / we look at the moon\u2014 / the way we used to see it / & settle down the stoicism. / we talk for years / & travel through time / & it feels so good\u2014 / we grow old together / I believe, maybe / we could have it all\u2014 / swinging my humbled / late nights & / heartbreaks at / an end story / unchanging.",
